/* combos-love.js — classic script; assigns to window.TD. No ES modules, so file:// works.
   What two cards say together in a reading about love and relationships. For now it covers the 231 pairs of two
   Major Arcana cards, keyed "idA|idB" in deck order like combos.js (see TD.pairKey in js/spreads.js);
   any other pair shows the general reading from combos.js, labelled "General reading".
   Written fresh for this demo; a live site edits or replaces them. Loaded only when a reading needs it. */
window.TD = window.TD || {};
window.TD.COMBOS_LOVE = {"major-00|major-01":"Fresh romantic energy and real social skill have arrived together. If you are single, start a conversation with someone you would normally only notice from across the room, and let your ease do the work. If you are partnered, surprise them with a plan you made yourself, not one you ordered.",
"major-00|major-02":"Your gut has been quietly answering a question your head keeps reopening. If you are single, notice who you feel calm around rather than who looks best on paper. If you are together, say the thing you have sensed but never spoken, gently and without accusation, and see how it lands.",
"major-00|major-03":"A new attachment grows best when both people feel looked after. If you are single, choose dates that feel nourishing, like a shared meal or a long walk, over ones designed to impress. If you are together, do one small tender thing for their comfort and yours, and skip the grand gesture.",
"major-00|major-04":"Openness wants a few ground rules. If you are single, know your non-negotiables before the first date so excitement cannot talk you out of them. If you are together, agree on how you will handle one practical thing you keep drifting on, such as time, chores or plans, and write the answer down.",
"major-00|major-05":"A brand-new connection may be moving toward a traditional shape, such as meeting families, marking milestones or sharing customs. If you are single, ask whether you truly want the familiar script or just assumed you should. If you are partnered, choose which rituals to keep and which to invent.",
"major-00|major-06":"You are being asked what you actually value, and honest answers matter more than chemistry alone. If you are single, decide two or three things you will not compromise on, then date with those in mind. If you are together, tell your partner one hope you have held back, and invite theirs.",
"major-00|major-07":"Excitement has found a direction, so the question is where you are heading, together or alone. If you are single, say what kind of relationship you want instead of drifting into whatever appears. If you are partnered, choose one shared goal for the next few months and check in on it monthly.",
"major-00|major-08":"New love, or a new phase of an old one, rewards gentleness over gusto. If you are single, let attraction grow at its own pace and be kind to your nerves on the first few dates. If you are together, meet a shaky moment with warmth rather than trying to win it, and watch how quickly tension eases.",
"major-00|major-09":"Before jumping into something new, a stretch of solitude may show you what you truly want from a partner. If you are single, treat time alone as useful rather than a waiting room, and finish one honest list of needs. If you are together, ask for a quiet evening and offer the same in return.",
"major-00|major-10":"Timing is doing part of the work here, and no amount of effort can hurry another person's readiness. If you are single, keep living your life so that chance can find you. If you are together, notice that a season is shifting and meet it with curiosity instead of resistance.",
"major-00|major-11":"Honest accounting is called for. If you are single, look fairly at your patterns: what you choose, what you overlook and what keeps repeating. If you are together, talk about whether the give and take feels even, using specific examples instead of scorekeeping. Fairness is a good foundation for anything new.",
"major-00|major-12":"A new stretch of love may ask you to slow down and see it from the other person's side. If you are single, resist pushing for a label this week and stay curious about who they really are. If you are together, describe their view of a recurring argument before you defend yours.",
"major-00|major-13":"An old pattern or relationship chapter is ending so something new can begin. If you are single, drop the story that you are behind or that the same disappointing type will keep turning up. If you are together, name one habit you are both ready to retire, and celebrate its going.",
"major-00|major-14":"New love does better at a steady simmer than a rolling boil. If you are single, let a connection unfold over several meetings without deciding too soon what it means. If you are together, mix novelty into your familiar routines one small change at a time, and see what blend suits you both.",
"major-00|major-15":"A new attraction may be tangled up with an old hook, such as a familiar type, a taste for intensity or a fear of being alone. If you are single, notice whether what pulls you feels warm or merely urgent. If you are together, name one stuck habit without blame.",
"major-00|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may clear away an assumption in your love life and leave room for something more honest. If you are single, let go of a hope built on wishes rather than facts, and stay open to a different kind of connection. If you are together, meet the rough patch with candor.",
"major-00|major-17":"Gentle hope returns after a sore patch. If you are single, trust again in small steps without demanding certainty from someone new. If you are together, do something quietly restorative as a pair, like a long walk or an evening without screens, and let closeness come back at its own speed.",
"major-00|major-18":"A hopeful new connection may be wrapped in half-facts and projected feelings. If you are single, enjoy the mystery without treating your imagination as evidence, and ask direct questions early. If you are together, say a worry aloud instead of letting it grow in private, and compare it with what your partner actually says.",
"major-00|major-19":"Warm, open, uncomplicated affection is on offer. If you are single, say yes to easy, cheerful invitations and let someone meet the sunny version of you. If you are together, plan something playful out in the open, like a day trip or a game night, and enjoy it without analyzing it.",
"major-00|major-20":"A call is asking you to review your romantic history honestly and then begin again as a wiser person. If you are single, forgive yourself and past partners for old mistakes, and date from what you learned. If you are together, revisit an old hurt, apologize where it is due and open a new chapter.",
"major-00|major-21":"One stage of your love story has finished properly, and you are free to begin another. If you are single, count what you learned from past relationships and carry it forward lightly. If you are together, celebrate what you have completed as a pair, then choose a new shared adventure to look forward to.",
"major-01|major-02":"Action and intuition together point to a relationship where you say what you feel and back it with what you do. If you are single, trust your gut about who deserves your time and make a move on it. If you are together, follow a quiet hunch with a direct, kind question.",
"major-01|major-03":"Attention and warmth grow a bond. If you are single, put your effort into dates that let you relax and enjoy the company, like a meal you cook together or a garden walk. If you are together, make something as a pair, such as a dinner or a home project, and look after each other's comfort as you do.",
"major-01|major-04":"Ideas and boundaries go hand in hand. If you are single, clarify what you want and where your limits are, then present yourself with confidence. If you are together, use your creativity to design a routine that works, such as a weekly plan for time together, and stick to it. Structure can make room for spontaneity.",
"major-01|major-05":"Charm works better when it rests on good foundations. If you are single, learn from couples you respect and notice which habits keep their relationships steady. If you are together, honor a tradition or ritual that matters to you both and add a personal twist. Old wisdom and fresh effort make a strong pair.",
"major-01|major-06":"You have real ability to shape your love life, and now comes the question of what you want. If you are single, choose based on values and honest attraction instead of ease. If you are together, make a clear, wholehearted choice to give your partner your attention, and say aloud what you are choosing.",
"major-01|major-07":"Intention and drive make a powerful pair. If you are single, decide what you want in a relationship and take active steps toward it, like joining a group or arranging a date. If you are together, agree on a shared direction and set a goal for the next few months. Steady aim beats scattered effort.",
"major-01|major-08":"Gentle skill outperforms force in relationships. If you are single, let your confidence show in a relaxed way, and let a slow start be fine. If you are together, handle a difficult moment calmly and skillfully, with warmth and no show of power. Steady, kind presence wins trust better than clever lines.",
"major-01|major-09":"Time apart, or quiet within a relationship, can sharpen what you offer. If you are single, spend a few evenings working out what you want, then return to dating with a clear question in hand. If you are together, ask for solitude without making it a statement about your partner, and share what you learned afterward.",
"major-01|major-10":"You can put yourself in the way of luck, and you cannot schedule it. If you are single, be visible and prepared with an open mind, by joining things you enjoy and starting conversations. If you are together, adapt to a change in circumstances as a team, using your best skills. Some timing is not in your hands.",
"major-01|major-11":"Honesty and fairness have consequences, and you have the skill to use them. If you are single, present yourself truthfully, without exaggeration, and expect the same. If you are together, discuss how decisions are shared, and give specific examples of what feels fair. Straightforward dealing is the most reliable way to build trust.",
"major-01|major-12":"A pause may work better than a push. If you are single, stop trying to engineer a meeting or a reply, and look at your dating life from a different angle. If you are together, try to see a recurring issue as your partner sees it, and set your solutions aside until you have listened fully.",
"major-01|major-13":"Ending something old is a creative act. If you are single, clear out habits, messages or expectations left over from a past relationship, and see what space opens. If you are together, agree to retire one pattern that no longer serves you, then decide together what to build in its place.",
"major-01|major-14":"Patience and small adjustments do more than dramatic gestures. If you are single, blend your life with someone else's slowly, and pay attention to how the mix feels. If you are together, test small changes in how you spend time or handle chores, then adjust the proportions until the balance suits you both.",
"major-01|major-15":"Your charm can serve you or trap you. If you are single, notice whether a pattern of flirting, testing or controlling keeps you from real closeness, and try being plain instead. If you are together, ask honestly what habit or need for control you both keep feeding, and loosen it together.",
"major-01|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may reveal that something was built on false footing. If you are single, take a breath and separate what was true about a past connection from what you wished were true. If you are together, meet the disruption with honesty, and rebuild on what was real between you.",
"major-01|major-17":"Hope is quiet and practical. If you are single, act on your trust that things can heal, with small steps like reaching out to a friend or trying a new activity. If you are together, do a modest repair, such as apologizing for something small or resuming a shared habit, and let goodwill return in its own time.",
"major-01|major-18":"Fog makes it easy to build on something imagined. If you are single, ask a new person direct questions about their availability and intentions, and check the answers against their actions. If you are together, confirm a worry with facts before acting on it. What is still murky deserves patience.",
"major-01|major-19":"Affection and honesty are on full display. If you are single, be openly yourself and enjoy meeting people without a script. If you are together, share your joy and your talents with your partner, and celebrate what is going well. There is nothing to hide, and being visible tends to draw good company.",
"major-01|major-20":"A call to use your abilities more fully may extend to your love life. If you are single, review your past relationships honestly, forgive what needs forgiving and date as the person you have become. If you are together, revisit a conversation you have put off, and answer it as your whole self.",
"major-01|major-21":"Something you started has come around to completion. If you are single, mark the end of a long chapter of searching or healing, and enjoy being whole before you begin again. If you are together, celebrate a milestone or shared goal, and write down what you learned about working as a team.",
"major-02|major-03":"Your body already knows how you feel about this person, or about this stretch of being alone. Before analyzing, notice what settles you and what tightens you. Then care for that feeling with something small and physical: a shared meal, a slow evening, a walk without your phone.",
"major-02|major-04":"Some feelings are hard to say and some boundaries are hard to hold, and you may be facing both. Name privately what you need, then put one clear limit into words. Private knowing gets sturdier once it has a shape. Single or partnered, a calm sentence beats a long silence.",
"major-02|major-05":"Inner knowing and shared expectations may not agree right now. Maybe family, culture or 'how relationships are supposed to go' pulls one way while your gut pulls another. Listen to both without rushing to pick. Talking with someone you trust about what you actually want can help sort borrowed rules from your own.",
"major-02|major-06":"A choice is forming, and your quietest feeling has the honest answer. Ask what you would choose if nobody were watching or judging. If you are single, that may mean deciding what kind of connection you want. If you are partnered, it may mean saying something you have kept private.",
"major-02|major-07":"Drive and stillness are pulling in different directions. One part of you wants to push things forward, and another says not yet. Slow down long enough to hear the second voice. Moving toward a person or a decision works better when your pace matches what you privately know.",
"major-02|major-08":"Gentle patience is the way in. A tender or guarded feeling, yours or someone else's, will not respond to pressure. Stay calm, stay kind, and let trust be earned slowly. If you are single, this can mean being gentle with your own pace of opening up.",
"major-02|major-09":"Time alone is doing real work right now. You may be sorting out what you want before you let anyone else weigh in. That is not avoidance if you come back with an honest answer. Give yourself a set stretch of solitude, then share what you found with someone safe.",
"major-02|major-10":"Things are shifting in ways you cannot force, and part of you already senses which way. Stop trying to control the timing. Listen for what feels true as circumstances change, and let it guide small choices. Single or attached, you can prepare without grasping.",
"major-02|major-11":"Honesty has to run both ways here, starting with the version you tell yourself. Look at what you have actually done, said and allowed, not just what you felt. Then speak plainly about it. Fairness in a relationship begins with an accurate inner ledger.",
"major-02|major-12":"A pause is not a failure. Something in the connection, or in you, needs to be held still so you can see it from another side. Resist filling the silence with quick answers. Ask yourself what looks different if you drop your usual story about it.",
"major-02|major-13":"Something in your emotional life is ready to end, and you probably felt it before you admitted it. Honor that quiet sense rather than arguing with it. Clearing out an old pattern, hope or habit leaves room. If you are single, that space may be the whole point.",
"major-02|major-14":"Slow, steady blending is what this asks for. Trust develops through small, repeated exchanges, not big declarations. Keep listening to your own feelings while making room for another person's. Go at an even pace, neither rushing nor freezing, and let closeness build.",
"major-02|major-15":"You know more about this pattern than you admit. Something keeps a hold on you, maybe a person, a habit or an old hurt, and part of you has already seen it. Say it aloud to someone safe. Naming the loop is the first step toward loosening it.",
"major-02|major-16":"A sudden jolt may confirm what your gut had been whispering. Something built on a shaky assumption falls, and the shock is real. Give yourself room to feel it. Afterward, notice that you had sensed the crack, and trust that sense earlier next time.",
"major-02|major-17":"Healing here happens quietly, out of sight. You do not have to announce that you are ready to open up again. Rest, be kind to yourself, and let trust return at its own speed. If you are single, hope can be a private and gentle thing.",
"major-02|major-18":"Feelings are muddy right now, and deciding tonight would only add to the fog. Notice what you keep dreaming about, hoping for or fearing, and keep it separate from what has really happened. Ask direct questions and write down the answers you get. Clarity comes with time.",
"major-02|major-19":"What you have felt privately can finally step into daylight. Warmth and honesty go together here: say the true thing cheerfully, without hedging. A relationship benefits from openness, and if you are single, being yourself in plain view is attractive. Enjoy simple time together.",
"major-02|major-20":"An honest review is due, and you already know what it will say. Look back at the whole story of this relationship or your time alone, then answer the call you have been hearing. Forgive what needs forgiving, including yourself, and decide what comes next.",
"major-02|major-21":"A long emotional cycle is nearing its close, and you understand it better than you did. Take time to acknowledge what you have learned about love and about yourself. Whether you are single or partnered, this is a moment for calm gratitude before the next chapter.",
"major-03|major-04":"Warmth and boundaries can support each other. Affection grows best where both people know what is expected and what is off the table. If you are together, talk about routines and limits kindly. If you are single, look for someone who is both caring and dependable.",
"major-03|major-05":"Old family patterns and traditions shape how you give and receive care. Notice what you inherited: how affection was shown, what was expected of partners. Keep the customs that nourish you and gently rewrite the ones that do not. Shared rituals can be a lovely way to bond.",
"major-03|major-06":"Affection and real choice come together here. You are being asked what you value in love, and your body and heart likely already lean one way. Choose the connection that feeds you, and treat it generously. Single or attached, care for what matters most to you.",
"major-03|major-07":"Care and momentum work together when you keep them in balance. You can move toward what you want while staying tender with yourself and others. Avoid pushing so hard that the relationship becomes another task. Let some plans be enjoyable rather than efficient.",
"major-03|major-08":"Tenderness is your strongest tool. With yourself or a partner, patience and kindness are what change things, not pressure. Let affection be steady and unshowy. If you are single, treat your own needs with the same gentleness you would offer a friend.",
"major-03|major-09":"Rest and solitude may be what nurture you most right now. Taking space is not rejection, it is refilling. Tell the people close to you what you need, and be kind to yourself about it. Sometimes the caring thing is a quiet evening with a lamp and a book.",
"major-03|major-10":"Seasons change in relationships, and this looks like a turn toward more abundance. Let good things come without gripping them. Enjoy what is present, and stay flexible about how it unfolds. If you are single, being open to unplanned meetings and ordinary kindness serves you well.",
"major-03|major-11":"Generosity works best when it is fair. Check whether giving and receiving are balanced between you and the other person. Care that only flows one way tends to sour. Speak honestly about what you need, and listen just as honestly.",
"major-03|major-12":"Slowing down lets affection deepen. You may be asked to hold still and let the relationship, or your feelings, ripen without pushing. See the situation from the other person's side. Sometimes the most loving act is to pause and wonder what they need.",
"major-03|major-13":"An old way of loving is ending so a fuller one can grow. Let go of a habit, role or hurt that has stopped nourishing you. Grieve what needs it, then clear space. If you are single, this can be a fresh start with yourself first.",
"major-03|major-14":"A balanced, nurturing rhythm is what serves you. Mix time together with time apart, talking with silence, giving with receiving. Do not rush the middle stretch. Steady, mild care will do more for a relationship, or for your own heart, than intense gestures.",
"major-03|major-15":"Comfort and craving can be hard to tell apart. Notice if something that feels like care is actually a habit that keeps you stuck, such as overgiving or overindulging. Ask what you need beneath the urge. Real nourishment leaves you freer, not more tied.",
"major-03|major-16":"A sudden shake-up may hit what felt safe and cozy. It is unsettling, and it can also clear away something that was not truly feeding you. Look after your basics: sleep, food, friends. Rebuild slowly with what is real and warm.",
"major-03|major-17":"Gentle recovery is underway. After a hard stretch, kindness toward your own body and heart brings hope back in small pieces. Let people care for you and accept it. If you are single, an open, unhurried heart makes room for good things without forcing them.",
"major-03|major-18":"Emotions are rich and a bit foggy. Fertile feelings can also stir old fears and fantasies. Look after your body with sleep and simple meals, and hold off on big conclusions. Ask for what is actually true instead of filling gaps with imagination.",
"major-03|major-19":"Warmth, fun and plain affection are on offer. Enjoy simple pleasures together or on your own: a good meal, sunshine, laughter. Let yourself be openly happy without waiting for a reason. Joy shared freely tends to invite more of it.",
"major-03|major-20":"A moment of honest review asks you to look at how you have loved, including how you have cared for yourself. Forgive where it is due. Then answer the call to live differently: more openly, more warmly. A renewed sense of worth changes how you show up.",
"major-03|major-21":"A loving chapter is coming to a full, satisfying close, or a relationship feels whole and well grown. Savor it. Give thanks, mark the moment together, and rest before you start anything new. If you are single, feeling complete on your own is real.",
"major-04|major-05":"Commitment and convention are in focus. You may be weighing what a serious relationship should look like: rules, roles, milestones. Talk openly about which traditions you both want and which you would rather write yourselves. Structure works when both people helped shape it.",
"major-04|major-06":"Choosing someone, or choosing to stay, takes both heart and firm boundaries. Decide what you value, then act on it consistently. Being clear about limits does not cool love, it steadies it. If you are single, know your standards before you meet anyone.",
"major-04|major-07":"Determination and discipline are strong, but relationships need softness too. Check whether you are steering the connection like a project. Agree on a direction together, and leave room for the other person to hold a rein. If you are single, aim at what you want without bulldozing.",
"major-04|major-08":"Firm and gentle can live in the same person. You can hold a boundary without hostility and stay warm while you do it. Try calm words rather than commands. In a relationship, this shows up as steady reliability that also feels safe.",
"major-04|major-09":"Time apart to think about your boundaries may be wise. Step back and ask what structure you need in love, what you can offer and what you cannot. Come back with a clear, honest statement. If you are single, this is a good season for defining your own standards.",
"major-04|major-10":"Even solid foundations sit inside changing seasons. You may want control, and life offers timing instead. Keep your commitments and boundaries steady while allowing feelings and circumstances to shift. Adaptability, paired with reliability, keeps a relationship strong.",
"major-04|major-11":"Fairness and clear terms matter now. Talk about expectations, responsibilities and boundaries with directness. Being consistent and accountable earns trust. If something is unbalanced, say so calmly and propose a fix. Honest rules make room for ease.",
"major-04|major-12":"Control is loosened by willingly pausing. Letting go of the need to steer can reveal what the other person actually needs. Set aside your plan for a while and listen. If you are single, stepping back from rigid expectations may help you notice something new.",
"major-04|major-13":"An old set of rules in your love life is ending. The roles or expectations you built may no longer fit. Let them go calmly and rebuild on honest ground. Singles can drop old standards that came from fear. Partners can write new agreements.",
"major-04|major-14":"Steady, balanced effort builds lasting love. Rules and routines work best when mixed with flexibility. Find a rhythm that suits both of you, and adjust it as life changes. Neither rigid control nor drifting will help. Moderation does.",
"major-04|major-15":"Control can look like security, and that is worth examining. Check whether rules, jealousy or a need to be in charge are holding the relationship in a tight grip, from either side. Real safety includes freedom. Loosen one demand and see what happens.",
"major-04|major-16":"Rigid arrangements can crack suddenly. If a relationship rested on control or unspoken rules, a jolt may expose it. It hurts, and it is also honest. Sort out what was solid and what was only held in place by pressure. Rebuild from the honest part.",
"major-04|major-17":"Hope needs a little structure to last. After a hard time, set gentle routines that help you heal, and keep honest boundaries with people. Trust can return through steady, reliable actions. Singles can hold an open heart alongside clear standards.",
"major-04|major-18":"Feelings are uncertain, and firm decisions now may rest on fog. Hold your boundaries but avoid ultimatums until things are clearer. Ask plain questions, expect plain answers, and notice when your imagination is filling in blanks. Patience protects you.",
"major-04|major-19":"Stability and joy sit comfortably together. A dependable, honest foundation lets happiness show up freely. Enjoy the ease of knowing where you stand. Singles can feel confident in clear values, and partners can celebrate what is working.",
"major-04|major-20":"It is time to review the terms you have been living by. Look honestly at your rules, roles and boundaries in love. Which have served you, and which were fear? Respond to the call to be more honest, and set one new agreement.",
"major-04|major-21":"Something stable and complete has been built. A long effort to create security in love is bearing fruit, or you have finished defining what you need. Appreciate the whole picture. Mark the accomplishment and enjoy the steadiness before the next chapter.",
"major-05|major-06":"Shared values and recognized commitment come into view. You may be thinking about what vows, traditions or family expectations mean to you. Choose what you honestly believe in rather than what is expected. Then say it aloud to your partner or to yourself.",
"major-05|major-07":"Following a known path can carry you forward. You may feel drawn to conventional milestones, and that is fine when they truly fit. Make sure you are steering, not just being carried. Agree on the route with your partner, and go together.",
"major-05|major-08":"Inherited beliefs about love can be met gently. If old rules, from family or culture, make you anxious or angry, soften toward them without obeying blindly. Patience with yourself and others opens space for new practices. Kindness is a tradition worth keeping.",
"major-05|major-09":"Stepping back from what everyone expects can clarify what you want. Take time alone to sort borrowed beliefs from your own. Reflect on your own ideas of commitment. Later, share your findings with someone wise, whether a friend, counselor or elder.",
"major-05|major-10":"Customs and timing collide. Perhaps people around you expect a schedule for relationships, but life is turning on its own clock. Keep the rituals that hold meaning and let go of pressure. Trust that steady values will carry you through changing seasons.",
"major-05|major-11":"Fair commitments matter more than fancy ones. Check whether the agreements you have, spoken or assumed, are honest and equal. If you follow rules from family or culture, ask whether they treat you fairly. Make your vows real by keeping them, in small ways.",
"major-05|major-12":"Setting aside the expected script allows a new view. You may be asked to pause the usual milestones and question them. Look at the relationship from a different angle. Sometimes stepping out of line for a while shows what you truly believe.",
"major-05|major-13":"An inherited way of doing love is ending. A belief, a role or a family script no longer fits. Let it go respectfully. You can honor what it gave while choosing something more honest. Singles and partners alike can rewrite the rules.",
"major-05|major-14":"Blend what you were taught with what you have lived. Take the best of the traditions you know and mix them with your own experience and your partner's. Go slowly, adjusting as you learn. Healthy commitment is built from steady compromise.",
"major-05|major-15":"Beliefs about how love must look may have become chains. Notice where expectations, guilt or shame keep you in a role that hurts. Question rules you never chose. Talk with someone outside the pattern, and take one step toward a freer arrangement.",
"major-05|major-16":"A belief you inherited about love or commitment may be cracking. It is shocking when a familiar script fails. Give yourself time to feel it. Later, ask which parts of the tradition were real and which were just habit, and rebuild with your own values.",
"major-05|major-17":"Faith in love can return through simple, trusted practices. A gentle ritual, a good conversation with a wise friend, or a shared tradition can restore hope. Take it slowly. Believing in good things again does not require certainty, just a small willingness.",
"major-05|major-18":"Unclear feelings meet familiar expectations. Do not let convention decide for you while you are unsure. Also do not let anxiety rewrite the story. Talk with someone steady and plain-spoken, and take time to see what is real before committing.",
"major-05|major-19":"Shared traditions bring gladness. Celebrations, family gatherings and easy rituals warm a relationship. Do the things that make you both smile. Singles can feel at home in community. Simple, open joy is a fine foundation.",
"major-05|major-20":"A call to reevaluate what you believe about love is loud now. Consider the lessons you were given, review your past, and decide which beliefs you keep. Forgive where needed. Then step into a commitment, or a solo season, that reflects your real convictions.",
"major-05|major-21":"A shared path reaches a celebrated milestone. A commitment, a tradition honored, or a long learning about love comes full circle. Mark it with people who matter. Feel the sense of belonging, then consider what comes next together or on your own.",
"major-06|major-07":"Decide, then move. You have weighed the choice long enough, and hesitation is now costing you. Pick what fits your values, and act on it with confidence. Partners can agree on a direction and steer together. Singles can take a real step.",
"major-06|major-08":"Love asks for courage and gentleness at once. Choose what you value, and stay patient with the messy parts of a real relationship. Handle your own fears kindly. Tenderness with a partner, or with yourself, is a quiet form of strength.",
"major-06|major-09":"A big choice about love deserves quiet thought. Step away from other people's advice, and ask yourself one honest question about what you want. Take time alone if you need it. The answer you find will be easier to live with.",
"major-06|major-10":"Choices meet circumstances. A meeting, a turning point or a change in timing may bring a decision to your door. You cannot control everything, but you can choose your response. Stay true to what you value as things shift.",
"major-06|major-11":"An honest, fair decision is needed. Look at the facts of the relationship as well as the feelings. Consider how your choices affect both of you. Take responsibility for your part. Clear, truthful communication builds real trust.",
"major-06|major-12":"A choice is on hold, and that pause may be wise. Resist forcing an answer. Look at the situation from your partner's side, or from the side of your future self. Sometimes the right choice becomes obvious after you stop pushing.",
"major-06|major-13":"A choice involves letting something go. To choose one path in love, you may have to end another: an old attachment, a habit, a fantasy. Grieve it, then commit to what you value. Clean endings allow honest beginnings.",
"major-06|major-14":"Harmony develops from patient, equal exchange. Two people, or two parts of you, learn to blend. Keep a steady pace and adjust as you learn each other. Compromise is not losing, it is how a shared life gets built.",
"major-06|major-15":"Attraction and attachment can look alike. Ask whether this connection reflects your values or is running on habit, craving or fear. Notice where you give up power. A healthy bond leaves you freer. Choose what helps you grow.",
"major-06|major-16":"A sudden event tests a relationship or reveals a mismatch. It can be painful, and it also cuts through pretense. After the shock, ask what you truly value. Rebuild, or begin again, on honest ground.",
"major-06|major-17":"Hope and honest connection go together. After a hard time, you can open up to love with clear values and a gentle heart. Trust returns bit by bit. Singles might feel a spark of quiet optimism. Partners can renew their commitment.",
"major-06|major-18":"Confusion clouds a choice. Feelings, dreams and worries mix, and it is hard to tell what is real. Avoid deciding tonight. Ask direct questions, watch actions over words, and give it time. What is true tends to show itself steadily.",
"major-06|major-19":"Open, joyful love is highlighted. A choice made from honest values brings ease. Enjoy each other's company, laugh, and be visible. Singles can bring genuine warmth to new meetings. Couples can simply celebrate what is good.",
"major-06|major-20":"It is time to answer honestly. Look back at your relationship story and choose accordingly. Forgive what needs forgiving, then commit to what you truly want, whether that means deepening a bond or living independently.",
"major-06|major-21":"A relationship, or a stage of self-discovery, reaches wholeness. Two halves feel integrated, or you feel complete on your own. Celebrate. Take time to enjoy the union and to appreciate the choices that led here.",
"major-07|major-08":"Determination softens into patience. Rather than pushing a relationship toward a result, steer with a light hand. Let feelings unfold and respond with calm. Whether single or attached, self-control paired with kindness beats forcing the pace.",
"major-07|major-09":"Slowing down from a rush toward love or an outcome may serve you. Pull over, take some solitude, and ask what you actually want. Then move again with clearer intent. Singles can use this pause to focus on self-knowledge.",
"major-07|major-10":"Momentum meets unpredictability. You are trying to steer, and events keep turning. Set your direction, but stay flexible about the route. Not everything in a relationship, or in finding one, follows your timetable. Adapt and keep going.",
"major-07|major-11":"Move forward honestly. Drive toward what you want, but check that you are treating others fairly along the way. Speak clearly and own the impact of your choices. A relationship gains steadiness when ambition and accountability travel together.",
"major-07|major-12":"Forward motion stops, and it may be for a reason. The urge to push a relationship along runs into a necessary pause. Use it to look at things differently. Willing patience now can prevent a rushed choice.",
"major-07|major-13":"A destination you were rushing toward may need to be let go. Endings redirect the journey. Grieve honestly, then choose a new heading. Singles may drop a chase that no longer fits. Partners can end a habit that slowed them.",
"major-07|major-14":"Steady pace wins. Instead of rushing toward a result, move at a moderate speed and keep blending your needs with another's. Small, consistent gestures beat dramatic bursts. Balance ambition with rest, and love has room to develop.",
"major-07|major-15":"Drive can turn compulsive. Check whether you are chasing someone or something out of habit, pride or fear. Real momentum feels chosen. Loosen the chain, take the reins back, and ask what you actually want.",
"major-07|major-16":"A sudden shock stops your momentum. A plan for a relationship, or your idea of it, is disrupted. It is jarring. Let yourself feel it, then check what you can salvage. New direction comes after the dust settles.",
"major-07|major-17":"Renewed hope gives you direction. After a difficult time, gently move toward what feels healing. Take small, steady steps. Singles can set an intention for the kind of love they hope for. Partners can plan something restorative together.",
"major-07|major-18":"You want to move things forward, but the picture is not clear yet. Slow down before you steer. Ask the plain question you have been avoiding, and notice whether your certainty comes from facts or from a mood. If you are single, do not rush toward someone you barely know.",
"major-07|major-19":"Effort and warmth are pulling the same way, which is rarer than it sounds. If you are partnered, choose one shared goal and go after it together, like a trip or a move. If you are single, showing up openly and with energy will serve you better than playing it cool.",
"major-07|major-20":"A moment of honest review asks where this relationship is heading, or what you truly want from dating. Stop drifting. Answer the call with a real conversation, then act on what you hear, even if that means changing course. Direction only counts once someone says it out loud.",
"major-07|major-21":"A long push is reaching its finish. Maybe you worked through a rough patch together, or you finally feel ready after time on your own. Enjoy arriving instead of hunting for the next challenge. Mark the moment with something small and shared, then ask what comes next.",
"major-08|major-09":"Gentleness needs some quiet to grow. Step back from the noise and ask yourself one honest question about what you need. Then bring the answer to your partner, or to your dating life, calmly. Patient self-knowledge makes you kinder and clearer with other people.",
"major-08|major-10":"Some of this is not yours to control, and gripping tighter will not help. Stay warm and steady while circumstances shift, whether that is distance, timing, or someone else's readiness. Offer patience to yourself as well. Let what is real prove itself over time.",
"major-08|major-11":"Kindness and fairness need to travel together here. Speak plainly about what each of you gives and receives, without scorekeeping or blame. Being gentle does not mean being silent. If you are single, look for someone whose actions match their words over many weeks.",
"major-08|major-12":"Waiting is fine when it is chosen and draining when it is not. Ask which this is. Try seeing the situation from your partner's side for a few days without arguing your case. If you are single, a pause can be a gift, provided you use it kindly.",
"major-08|major-13":"An ending is here, and you can meet it without hardening. Grieve honestly, be gentle with yourself, and do not rush to fill the space. If a chapter with a partner is changing form, courage looks like calm truth. If you are single, clearing old hurt makes room.",
"major-08|major-14":"Good relationships are built in the long middle, and this pair knows it. Small daily kindnesses, moderate reactions, and a steady temper do more than grand gestures. If you are single, notice who is easy to be patient with and who blends well with your ordinary life.",
"major-08|major-15":"A pattern has a grip on you, and force will not break it. Notice what you keep returning to even though it costs you, then face it with compassion instead of shame. Small honest steps beat dramatic vows. Ask a friend you trust to hold you accountable.",
"major-08|major-16":"A sudden shake-up tests how steady you are, so react slowly. Something false is falling, perhaps a story you told yourself or a promise that was never solid. Stay kind, protect your dignity, and let the dust settle before you decide what to rebuild.",
"major-08|major-17":"Healing is under way, and it rewards gentle persistence. Keep offering small kindnesses to yourself and to a partner. If you are single after a hard chapter, trust returns gradually. Hope does not need to be loud to be real, and it grows when you keep tending it.",
"major-08|major-18":"Unclear feelings, yours or theirs, tempt you to force an answer. Do the opposite. Stay calm, let your intuition speak without turning it into a story, and give things time to become visible. Be patient with your fears without letting them make the decisions.",
"major-08|major-19":"Warmth comes easily when you are relaxed with yourself. Enjoy the simple good: laughter, affection, an unforced day together. If you are single, your quiet confidence is attractive, so let yourself be seen. Being open usually costs less than you fear.",
"major-08|major-20":"An honest review is calling. Look at how you have handled your own fears and reactions, and answer with courage rather than defensiveness. Forgive yourself for the rough patches, then have the talk that clears the air. A deeper level of trust becomes possible.",
"major-08|major-21":"Patience has carried you to a place of wholeness. Whether partnered or single, you may feel complete in a way that does not depend on anyone's approval. Celebrate that steadiness, and let it shape what you choose next. Nothing is missing from today.",
"major-09|major-10":"Time alone is not a detour right now, it is part of the turn. Use the quiet to work out what you truly want, because circumstances are shifting. If you are together, ask your partner for space without leaving. If you are single, do not force the timing.",
"major-09|major-11":"Sit alone with a fair question: what have I contributed to this, and what do I deserve? Answer without excuses. That honesty prepares you for a straight conversation with a partner, or a wiser choice about who to date next.",
"major-09|major-12":"Both figures are withdrawn, so this is a rest, not a rejection. Let a stalled situation stay quiet a little longer. Use the still time to look at your habits from the outside. If you are single, a deliberate pause can be a healthy choice, not a failure.",
"major-09|major-13":"An ending invites a stretch of solitude, and that is fine. Give yourself time to sit with what is over without rushing into the next connection. The lamp you carry will show what you want next. Partners can do this inside a relationship, too.",
"major-09|major-14":"Quiet time and gentle balance work well together. Reflect alone, then blend what you learn slowly into your relationship or your dating life. No dramatic announcements are needed. Small adjustments in how you listen and share space will show your growth.",
"major-09|major-15":"Turn the lamp on a habit that holds you. Perhaps it is a pattern with a certain type of person, or a dependence you have excused. Look at it alone and honestly. Seeing it clearly is not punishment, it is how the chain begins to loosen.",
"major-09|major-16":"After a sudden jolt, retreat for a while. You do not owe anyone an instant explanation or a new plan. Sit quietly with what fell, and notice what was never solid. Your lamp will show what is still worth building on.",
"major-09|major-17":"A quiet period is turning toward hope. Time alone has helped you heal, and a gentle openness is returning. You do not need to rush toward anyone. Let your own light steady you, and it will draw the kind of company that suits it.",
"major-09|major-18":"You are searching in dim light, and it is easy to mistake shadows for facts. Go quiet, write down what you actually know versus what you fear, and hold off on big conclusions. Clarity with a partner comes from steady questions, not guesses.",
"major-09|major-19":"Solitude has turned into contentment. Whether you are single or partnered, you feel at ease with yourself, and that shows. Share your happiness simply. A relationship gains a lot from someone who knows their own mind and enjoys their own company.",
"major-09|major-20":"The lamp reveals a truth you have half known. Hear it, and respond. It might be that you are ready to commit, to leave a pattern behind, or to be honest about what you want. Calmly answering this call is worth more than another year of wondering.",
"major-09|major-21":"A period of self-discovery reaches a natural finish. You know yourself better, and that shows in how you relate. If you are single, you can meet others from wholeness, not need. If you are partnered, share what you have learned.",
"major-10|major-11":"Fate and fairness meet. Things are turning, and what you have put into a relationship is coming back in kind. Be honest and act decently while the wheel moves. If you are single, how you treat people now shapes who is around you later.",
"major-10|major-12":"Things are turning, yet you feel stuck. Accept that some timing is not yours to hurry. Use the wait to see your situation from another side, perhaps your partner's. If you are single, let the pause teach you what you want, instead of what you think you should want.",
"major-10|major-13":"A cycle is closing and another is beginning. It may feel like loss, but it is also movement. Let an old pattern or connection finish. Endings in love create room for something truer. Take care of yourself while things turn, and stay open to what arrives.",
"major-10|major-14":"Slow blending beats sudden fireworks while circumstances shift. Adjust your pace to the season you are in, and mix openness with patience. Small, steady adaptations with a partner keep things balanced. If you are single, let connections grow at a moderate temperature instead of forcing heat.",
"major-10|major-15":"The wheel keeps turning through the same pattern. Ask why the same kind of situation keeps returning, and what in it holds you. The cycle is not fate, it is a habit dressed as fate. Change one choice and the rotation changes.",
"major-10|major-16":"A sharp turn arrives and old arrangements do not survive it. It may feel unfair, and part of it is simply timing. Look at what was already shaky. You are not powerless: choose how you respond, and rebuild with more honesty than before.",
"major-10|major-17":"After a hard turn, hope returns. Luck seems to be shifting, and you may feel gently optimistic again. Nurture that feeling with honesty and small steps. If you are single, let yourself meet people through ordinary life. If you are partnered, share your renewed trust.",
"major-10|major-18":"Changes are underway, but you cannot see them clearly yet. Avoid acting on moods or midnight worries. Give things time to show their shape, and ask for honest words instead of guessing. Your intuition is useful, but check it against what is actually said and done.",
"major-10|major-19":"Good timing and plain happiness line up. Things feel lucky and easy, so enjoy them with gratitude. If you are single, say yes to invitations and let joy lead. If you are partnered, celebrate together, and remember to appreciate the ordinary good days too.",
"major-10|major-20":"A turning point calls for an honest answer. The situation is moving, and you feel a summons to decide who you want to be within it. Speak the truth you have been holding. Whatever the reply, you will know where you stand.",
"major-10|major-21":"A full cycle closes gracefully. What began some time ago has run its course and reached a satisfying place. Look back with gratitude. If you are single, you feel whole and ready for a new turn. If you are partnered, celebrate how far you have come.",
"major-11|major-12":"A fair decision cannot be rushed, so wait with open eyes. Consider your partner's viewpoint as carefully as your own. If you are single, a pause lets you see clearly what you owe yourself. When you do speak, your words will be balanced.",
"major-11|major-13":"An ending is the fair result of choices made, and it is time to accept it. Be honest about what happened and your part in it, without cruelty toward anyone. Closing the account cleanly lets you begin something new with clean hands.",
"major-11|major-14":"Fairness and gentleness balance each other. Talk about needs and limits in measured, honest words. Neither of you needs to win. If you are single, seek someone whose give and take feels even over time, not only at the start.",
"major-11|major-15":"Look honestly at an unequal arrangement. Something in the relationship, or in your pattern of choosing partners, keeps you tied to a bad deal. Seeing it clearly is the first step. You are allowed to ask for fairness and to step away from terms that never worked.",
"major-11|major-16":"A hard truth arrives suddenly and rearranges things. What was hidden is now visible, and consequences follow. It hurts, but it is also clarifying. Respond honestly, avoid revenge, and keep your integrity while you decide what to keep.",
"major-11|major-17":"Honesty leads to healing. Once you and your partner face what is true, hope grows naturally. If you are single, a fair look at past patterns clears the ground for gentler expectations. Trust is rebuilt by consistent, truthful acts, and it is possible.",
"major-11|major-18":"You are trying to judge something that is not yet clear. Avoid deciding on a mood or a partial story. Ask for the facts, listen without defending, and hold off on verdicts. Fairness needs good information, and the fog lifts with time.",
"major-11|major-19":"Honesty feels good here. Open, fair dealing brings warmth and ease. You and your partner can speak plainly without fear, and it draws you closer. If you are single, transparent people are the ones worth your time, and you can be one yourself.",
"major-11|major-20":"This is a moment of true accounting. You see what has happened and answer for it. Speak honestly, listen equally, and forgive where you can. It may reset the relationship on a truer footing, or help you close a chapter with clarity.",
"major-11|major-21":"Fair dealing has brought things to a satisfying whole. What you put in has been balanced by what you received. Enjoy the sense of completeness, and be grateful. If you are single, you carry a clear conscience into whatever comes next.",
"major-12|major-13":"The pause and the ending belong together. Let go of the need to force outcomes. Something that no longer fits is dissolving, and resisting only prolongs the ache. Take a different view of what this loss makes possible, then step forward slowly.",
"major-12|major-14":"Patience is easy to say and hard to do, yet both cards ask for it. Let things develop at their own pace. Keep your side gentle and balanced while you wait, and be curious about your partner's rhythm. If you are single, unhurried connection is the healthy kind.",
"major-12|major-15":"Feeling stuck may be less about waiting and more about attachment. Ask whether you are pausing for a good reason or simply clinging to a pattern. A change of viewpoint can show that the chains are looser than they look.",
"major-12|major-16":"Sudden change forces you to stop and reconsider. Upheaval has interrupted the usual story. Rather than rushing to rebuild, hang in the uncomfortable pause and look at things from a new side. What seemed solid may have been a habit.",
"major-12|major-17":"Rest brings renewal. After an uncertain or tender time, you begin to feel hopeful without needing an answer. Allow yourself to trust slowly. If you are single, tending your own wellbeing is exactly the right thing to do right now.",
"major-12|major-18":"Waiting in the fog is uncomfortable. You do not have enough clarity and cannot force it. Try a different angle: write down your fears, then question each one. Give the situation time to reveal itself, and be patient with your own uncertainty.",
"major-12|major-19":"Here is a pause that turns out to be good. Letting go of control brings unexpected ease and warmth. Enjoy the stillness without demanding progress. If you are single, contentment while you wait draws better company than anxious searching does.",
"major-12|major-20":"A willing pause leads to an awakening. In the stillness you hear something honest about what you want. Answer it. It may mean forgiving a past hurt, or speaking up at last. Nothing needs to be forced: the call becomes clear when you listen.",
"major-12|major-21":"A voluntary wait has been worthwhile. Letting things unfold has led to a sense of completeness. Enjoy where you have arrived, and thank yourself for the patience. Whether you are single or partnered, you are ready for what comes next.",
"major-13|major-14":"After an ending, healing proceeds slowly. Do not hurry to fill the space. Mix rest with gentle activity, and allow trust to return in small doses. If you are in a relationship, changes may need gradual blending rather than a single dramatic break.",
"major-13|major-15":"Something is ending, and something else wants to keep you from letting it end. Notice the fear or habit that ties you to what is finished. Loosening that grip is painful and freeing. You deserve a life not built on obligation or repetition.",
"major-13|major-16":"This is a complete and sudden clearing. What ends does so abruptly and leaves little to hold. It is painful, and it is also honest. Give yourself space to grieve, avoid quick fixes, and rebuild only what is true when you are ready.",
"major-13|major-17":"After loss, hope. A quiet, tender renewal follows what has ended. You may be surprised how light you feel. Be open to gentle beginnings, and do not compare them to what was. If you are single, trust that new connection can arrive in its own way.",
"major-13|major-18":"An ending has left you in uncertainty. You are not sure what comes next, or what you truly feel. Let things stay unresolved for a while. Do not fill the gap with guesses. Journals, quiet walks, and honest talks with friends will help you see.",
"major-13|major-19":"Endings can be a relief. A weight is lifting, and you feel more like yourself. Enjoy the simple pleasure of a clear slate. If you are single, new warmth is possible. If you are partnered, letting an old pattern die can bring back real joy.",
"major-13|major-20":"This is a final accounting and a rebirth. See what has ended for what it was, forgive what you can, and answer the call to begin differently. It may involve a frank talk. You are allowed to become someone new.",
"major-13|major-21":"A cycle ends because it is complete, not because it failed. Honor what it gave you. You have grown, and you are ready for a new form of love, whether shared or solo. Let the close be peaceful, and thank the past for its part.",
"major-14|major-15":"Moderation is the antidote to a pattern that has you. Rather than swinging between craving and cutting off, look for the middle: healthy limits, honest talk, slow change. If you are single, notice whether excitement is hiding something unbalanced.",
"major-14|major-16":"A sudden break interrupts a calm patch. Answer with steadiness. Do not act on the first surge of feeling. Blend patience with honesty as you sort out what remains. Gentle, measured steps rebuild trust better than dramatic ones.",
"major-14|major-17":"Healing and hope work well together. Take things at a gentle pace, and let trust return naturally. If you are single, being kind to yourself sets the tone for what you attract. In a relationship, share small acts of care regularly.",
"major-14|major-18":"You feel unsure, and the cure is calm. Do not chase certainty through drama. Move slowly, ask gentle questions, and give feelings time to settle. Trust what stays consistent across days, rather than what flares at night.",
"major-14|major-19":"Ease and warmth arrive together. Things feel natural, balanced, and good. Enjoy simple routines shared with someone, or content time on your own. If you are single, relax: connections formed in good spirits tend to be sustainable.",
"major-14|major-20":"A gentle but real reckoning is here. Look at how you have been mixing your needs and your partner's over time, and adjust. The call is to be honest without harshness. Reconciling differences takes patience and clear words.",
"major-14|major-21":"Patient blending has led to wholeness. What you and someone else, or you and your own life, have been building slowly now feels complete. Appreciate it. Keep the small habits that got you here, because they are what made it last.",
"major-15|major-16":"A grip is broken suddenly. A pattern, a dependency, or a situation that felt inescapable collapses. It can be frightening and also freeing. Take care of yourself, be honest about what held you, and choose slowly what to build now.",
"major-15|major-17":"Hope shines on what has bound you. You can begin to loosen the pattern, and gentle self-care matters more than willpower. If you are single, believing you deserve better is a real starting point. Take one small, kind step away from what drains you.",
"major-15|major-18":"Fear and confusion feed each other here. Anxiety may distort what you see, and old habits pull you back. Get outside opinions from people you trust. Separate facts from fears. Clarity loosens the hold. You are free to take things slowly until the picture is clearer.",
"major-15|major-19":"Joy breaks a pattern. What once felt binding loses its power in honest warmth. Let simple, open happiness show you what you really want. If you are single, you no longer need to settle for what drains you.",
"major-15|major-20":"This is an honest awakening. You hear the call to leave a pattern behind, to forgive yourself, and to choose differently. Say what is true. Old bonds lose their force once you name them, and a new stage of life can begin.",
"major-15|major-21":"Freedom arrives at the end of a long tangle. The cycle is finishing, and you can stand on your own feet. Whatever bound you has run its course. Celebrate, and be careful not to recreate the same pattern in the next chapter.",
"major-16|major-17":"Calm comes after the storm. What fell was false, and the quiet that follows brings hope. Heal gently and let trust rebuild slowly. If you are single, be kind to yourself and look forward. New beginnings are possible without denying what happened.",
"major-16|major-18":"A shock has left you unsure what is real. Shadows and worries multiply after a sudden change. Wait before drawing conclusions. Find steady people to talk with, and ask for facts. Your footing will return as things settle.",
"major-16|major-19":"The storm ends and light returns. What broke made room for something truer and warmer. Allow yourself relief and joy. If you are single, you may feel freer than you expected. If you are partnered, honesty after a rough moment can bring you closer.",
"major-16|major-20":"A sudden truth demands a response. Something broke, and now you must decide what it means. Hear the call honestly. This can be a painful but clean turning point, giving you a chance to start over with clearer values.",
"major-16|major-21":"A dramatic ending completes a long story. What falls now was ready to fall, and what remains is whole. Honor the journey. Whether you are single or partnered, you are entering a new phase with hard-won wisdom.",
"major-17|major-18":"Hope shines through uncertainty. You might not have every answer, but a gentle faith persists. Follow your intuition carefully, and check it against real words and actions. If you are single, be open without being naive.",
"major-17|major-19":"Warmth, healing, and simple happiness are all present. Things feel bright and hopeful, and you deserve to enjoy them. If you are single, you radiate approachability. If you are partnered, spend time together doing what you both love.",
"major-17|major-20":"Hope answers a call. You feel ready to heal, forgive, and start fresh. Trust the inner voice urging you toward a more honest, open life. Speak your truth kindly, and let renewal begin. Whether you are single or partnered, the fresh start begins with how you treat yourself.",
"major-17|major-21":"Healing is complete, and hope has led somewhere whole. You feel at peace, whether partnered or on your own. Give thanks, share your contentment, and step into the next season with openness. Contentment you already feel is a good place to meet someone new or to grow closer to someone you have.",
"major-18|major-19":"The fog lifts and you see clearly. Worries that seemed large turn out to be manageable. Speak plainly about what confused you, and enjoy the relief. If you are single, trust yourself more. If you are partnered, honest talk brings warmth.",
"major-18|major-20":"A quiet call rises from the depths. Your dreams and feelings are pointing to something you can no longer ignore. Listen, and then act on it with care. Talk honestly, and let the fog clear as you speak.",
"major-18|major-21":"You are nearly there, though some doubts remain. Finish the current stage without letting vague worries spoil it. Enjoy what is real. Whole and satisfied feelings are possible even when a few questions stay unanswered.",
"major-19|major-20":"Joy and honesty combine. You are ready to embrace a truer way of loving. Forgive, speak openly, and celebrate. If you are single, awakening to your own worth draws warm and sincere connection. If you are in a relationship, say out loud what you are grateful for in each other.",
"major-19|major-21":"Happiness and wholeness arrive at once. You feel content, celebrated, and complete. Whether you are single or partnered, savor it and share it with people you trust. Say thank you out loud. Gratitude keeps good things bright.",
"major-20|major-21":"This is the final answer to a long question. You heard the call, responded honestly, and now a cycle completes. Enjoy the peace of no longer wondering. New beginnings can follow from this settled place."};
